<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31526" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nyctălops</span></b> ,
		ōpis, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νυκτάλωψ</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>That cannot see in the twilight</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 28,
				11, 47, § 170</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 50, 76, §
			203</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Dig. 21, 1, 10</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>That sees only at night</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nyctalopas, qui per noctem vident et per diem
					obscuritatem patiuntur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Theod. Prisc. 1, 10</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>The plant</i> nyctegretos, <i><span class="en">Plin. 21,
				11, 36, § 62</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
